WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.960
There are 440,000 children in&nbsp;
our foster care system right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.120
and almost every state reports that there is a&nbsp;
shortage of families willing to care for them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.240
Fortunately, in recent years, a growing number&nbsp;
of churches and faith-based organizations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.600
have revolutionized the way we recruit, train,&nbsp;
and support families. First, these churches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.080
understood that sharing a picture of a foster&nbsp;
child on the nightly news was not very effective.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.440
Instead, their pastors have begun telling their&nbsp;
congregations about children in their zip code&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.240
who need homes now. Second, they began to&nbsp;
offer training sessions at more convenient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.560
times and places, and they supplemented that&nbsp;
training with a religious understanding of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.760
the importance of caring for these children.&nbsp;
Finally, they provided a supportive community.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.960
Half of foster parents quit within the first&nbsp;
year, many because they are working in a vacuum.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.440
So these communities recruited&nbsp;
volunteers to offer respite care,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.240
help build furniture at the last minute, and&nbsp;
provide spiritual support to foster families.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.800
Other communities can learn a lot from these&nbsp;
examples. Would you consider fostering a child&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:14.000
in need? Let us know in our poll. Also, let us&nbsp;
know what other topics you'd like our scholars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.840
to cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and&nbsp;
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

